      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Not all of the options meet the requirements for custom fallback, but a good chunk of them do. Probably not difficult for rpm site to say something about the polygon count.\n\nI wonder if any improvements have been made to rpm VRChat or if it's just been sitting since implemented.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-13T15:42:46.261Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Please allow RPM Avatars to be assigned as Fallback Avatars from the Menu with a button.\n\nReady Player Me Avatars are fallback and Quest compatible already. \n\nMany people are not aware of their fallback avatar nor they care or don't have the time to make a custom Fallback avatar so it doesn't look like the public ones that don't really match their current Poor/Very Poor avatar.\n\nBecause of that I guess some people still prefer to see a boring half bodied robot instead. It's funny to see a room full of fallbacks currently but that fun only lasts some time. And some avatars are too wide or big already and that is added in top of their big custom avatars.\n\nMaking it easy to setup RPM Avatars as Fallback could bring another level of immersion for those who don't want to see robots, neither a room full of monsters but still want to see \"people\". And a look-a-like RPM avatar would be the closest to match their Poor or Very Poor avatars. (Unless their representative avatar is not human looking, like a furry for example).\n\nThis would also work as solution in the meantime for those who are planning but haven't uploaded their custom Fallback.\n\nI asked around about this idea and most of my friends seem to like it.",
